Decision 2028/AIO-16, adopted 2028-08-21, effective 2028-10-01.

Subject: minimum documentation for third-party evaluation access under Article 55.

Any evaluation-access submission relied upon in the Article 55 procedure opened 2027-04-15 — or in a Union conformity assessment — must include:
(a) a written sandbox specification, including network and tool access restrictions;
(b) a blast-radius analysis covering plausible real-world effects of the subject model's actions during evaluation (see AIID #1628);
(c) identification of an external observer holding stop authority over the evaluation run;
(d) notification of serious incidents arising during the run through the channels established under Decision 2027/AIO-11.

Scope: evaluations conducted in the Union, or whose results are relied upon in the Union. Submissions lacking these elements will be recorded as incomplete and the 60-day assessment clock under Decision 2028/AIO-14 will not start.

Templates: published today alongside the Decision 2027/AIO-11 package. Alignment: drafted to be readable against the UK AISI 60-day findings rule (2028-05-01) and China CAC incident reporting (2028-06-01), so the three regimes can be compared without translation.
